s had been flooded?","start":11.84,"end":17.48,"score":0.924,"timingValid":true,"needsReview":false,"reviewReasons":[]},{"id":"b3-010-002","sourceId":"b3-010-002","sourceIndex":1,"part":1,"parts":1,"wordRange":[0,14],"wordModel":"english-ctc-fallback","text":"The great ship, Titanic sailed for New York from Southampton on April 10th, 1912.","start":20.18,"end":28.34,"score":0.983,"timingValid":true,"needsReview":false,"reviewReasons":[]},{"id":"b3-010-003","sourceId":"b3-010-003","sourceIndex":2,"part":1,"parts":1,"wordRange":[0,11],"wordModel":"english-ctc-fallback","text":"She was carrying 1, 316 passengers and a crew of 891.","start":29.49,"end":36.4,"score":0.986,"timingValid":true,"needsReview":false,"reviewReasons":[]},{"id":"b3-010-004","text":"Even by modern standards, the 46, 000 ton Titanic was a colossal ship.","start":37.913,"end":43.883,"score":0.925,"timingValid":true,"needsReview":true,"sourceId":"b3-010-004","sourceIndex":3,"part":1,"parts":1,"wordRange":[0,13],"wordModel":"legacy-review","reviewReasons":["unresolved-word-alignment"]},{"id":"b3-010-005-p01","sourceId":"b3-010-005","sourceIndex":4,"part":1,"parts":2,"wordRange":[0,16],"wordModel":"mms-fa","text":"At that time, however, she was not only the largest ship that had ever been built,","start":45.06,"end":50.03,"score":0.994,"timingValid":true,"needsReview":false,"reviewReasons":[]},{"id":"b3-010-005-p02","sourceId":"b3-010-005","sourceIndex":4,"part":2,"parts":2,"wordRange":[16,27],"wordModel":"mms-fa","text":"but was regarded as unsinkable, for she had sixteen water-tight compartments.","start":50.46,"end":56.57,"score":0.919,"timingValid":true,"needsReview":false,"reviewReasons":[]},{"id":"b3-010-006","sourceId":"b3-010-006","sourceIndex":5,"part":1,"parts":1,"wordRange":[0,14],"wordModel":"mms-fa","text":"Even if two of these were flooded, she would still be able to float.","start":57.71,"end":61.89,"score":0.948,"timingValid":true,"needsReview":false,"reviewReasons":[]},{"id":"b3-010-007-p01","sourceId":"b3-010-007","sourceIndex":6,"part":1,"parts":2,"wordRange":[0,11],"wordModel":"mms-fa","text":"The tragic sinking of this great liner will always be remembered,","start":63.1,"end":66.98,"score":0.966,"timingValid":true,"needsReview":false,"reviewReasons":[]},{"id":"b3-010-007-p02","sourceId":"b3-010-007","sourceIndex":6,"part":2,"parts":2,"wordRange":[11,24],"wordModel":"mms-fa","text":"for she went down on her first voyage with heavy loss of life.","start":67.4,"end":71.66,"score":0.981,"timingValid":true,"needsReview":false,"reviewReasons":[]},{"id":"b3-010-008-p01","sourceId":"b3-010-008","sourceIndex":7,"part":1,"parts":2,"wordRange":[0,18],"wordModel":"mms-fa","text":"Four days after setting out, while the Titanic was sailing across the icy waters of the North Atlantic,","start":73.49,"end":80.1,"score":0.971,"timingValid":true,"needsReview":false,"reviewReasons":[]},{"id":"b3-010-008-p02","sourceId":"b3-010-008","sourceIndex":7,"part":2,"parts":2,"wordRange":[18,27],"wordModel":"mms-fa","text":"a huge iceberg was suddenly spotted by a lookout.","start":80.89,"end":84.28,"score":0.969,"timingValid":true,"needsReview":false,"reviewReasons":[]},{"id":"b3-010-009","sourceId":"b3-010-009","sourceIndex":8,"part":1,"parts":1,"wordRange":[0,16],"wordModel":"mms-fa","text":"After the alarm had been given, the great ship turned sharply to avoid a direct collision.","start":85.77,"end":92.35,"score":0.986,"timingValid":true,"needsReview":false,"reviewReasons":[]},{"id":"b3-010-010-p01","sourceId":"b3-010-010","sourceIndex":9,"part":1,"parts":2,"wordRange":[0,6],"wordModel":"english-ctc-fallback","text":"The Titanic turned just in time,","start":93.51,"end":96.3,"score":0.988,"timingValid":true,"needsReview":false,"reviewReasons":[]},{"id":"b3-010-010-p02","sourceId":"b3-010-010","sourceIndex":9,"part":2,"parts":2,"wordRange":[6,24],"wordModel":"english-ctc-fallback","text":"narrowly missing the immense wall of ice which rose over 100 feet out of the water beside her.","start":96.72,"end":103.06,"score":0.979,"timingValid":true,"needsReview":false,"reviewReasons":[]},{"id":"b3-010-011","sourceId":"b3-010-011","sourceIndex":10,"part":1,"parts":1,"wordRange":[0,19],"wordModel":"mms-fa","text":"Suddenly, there was a slight trembling sound from below, and the captain went down to see what had happened.","start":104.51,"end":111.53,"score":0.987,"timingValid":true,"needsReview":false,"reviewReasons":[]},{"id":"b3-010-012","sourceId":"b3-010-012","sourceIndex":11,"part":1,"parts":1,"wordRange":[0,16],"wordModel":"mms-fa","text":"The noise had been so faint that no one thought that the ship had been damaged.","start":112.72,"end":117.58,"score":0.984,"timingValid":true,"needsReview":false,"reviewReasons":[]},{"id":"b3-010-013-p01","sourceId":"b3-010-013","sourceIndex":12,"part":1,"parts":2,"wordRange":[0,13],"wordModel":"english-ctc-fallback","text":"Below, the captain realized to his horror that the Titanic was sinking rapidly,","start":118.54,"end":123.83,"score":0.981,"timingValid":true,"needsReview":false,"reviewReasons":[]},{"id":"b3-010-013-p02","sourceId":"b3-010-013","sourceIndex":12,"part":2,"parts":2,"wordRange":[13,24],"wordModel":"english-ctc-fallback","text":"for five of her sixteen watertight compartments had already been flooded!","start":124.53,"end":129.65,"score":0.968,"timingValid":true,"needsReview":false,"reviewReasons":[]},{"id":"b3-010-014","sourceId":"b3-010-014","sourceIndex":13,"part":1,"parts":1,"wordRange":[0,16],"wordModel":"mms-fa","text":"The order to abandon ship was given and hundreds of people plunged into the icy water.","start":130.58,"end":135.65,"score":0.976,"timingValid":true,"needsReview":false,"reviewReasons":[]},{"id":"b3-010-015","sourceId":"b3-010-015","sourceIndex":14,"part":1,"parts":1,"wordRange":[0,13],"wordModel":"english-ctc-fallback","text":"As there were not enough life-boats for everybody, 1, 500 lives were lost.","start":136.25,"end":141.87,"score":0.976,"timingValid":true,"needsReview":false,"reviewReasons":[]}]}
